@cortexkit/pi-magic-context 0.41.3
Source: https://github.com/cortexkit/magic-context (packages/pi-plugin)
Package metadata: license MIT, author "ualtinok".

The published npm package declares MIT but its `files` list contains only
`dist/` and `README.md`, so the tarball has no LICENSE file. This directory
ships the standard MIT text with a generic copyright-holder line rather than
inventing a year or name. If the upstream repository license becomes available,
replace LICENSE with that file verbatim.

Included files (approximately 3.3 MB total, 10 files):
  package.json                     upstream manifest (version/license/peer metadata)
  LICENSE                          MIT text
  NOTICE                           this file
  dist/index.js                    1,434 KB extension entry
  dist/index-s0zw9ddk.js           1,801 KB shared SQLite/schema/context core
  dist/index-147qn1yq.js              15 KB storage, logger, data paths
  dist/index-22jkk6wg.js             1.4 KB module resolution helper
  dist/index-b3eqj1g6.js             1.6 KB notification helper
  dist/fynvra-pi-tui-stub.js         Fynvra host stub
  dist/fynvra-host.js               Fynvra async lifecycle / SDK facade bridge

Why this cannot be reduced to only the compaction functions: `index.js` statically
imports the shared core (`index-s0zw9ddk.js`) for the SQLite schema, config
schema, compartment storage, tag/drop engine and historian prompts; that core is
a 1.8 MB bundled chunk. Splitting it would mean rewriting/vendoring the entire
Magic Context runtime, which this integration deliberately avoids. The omitted
chunks are the large optional features: `index-e7vx3byk.js` (2,420 KB quickjs),
`transformers*.js` (875-1,034 KB each, ONNX/embedding), plus subagent-entry.js,
historian-calibration-extension.js and OMP/OpenCode TUI helpers. Fynvra disables
embedding/dreamer/sidekick/smart-notes and runs the historian in-process, so those
modules are never imported.

Local patches (initial patches are numbered in the source; hosted guards also
use fynvra-prefixed helpers and MAGIC_CONTEXT_FYNVRA_HOST checks):
   1. PiSubagentRunner.run delegates to the Fynvra in-process runner.
   2. loadPiConfig uses MAGIC_CONTEXT_CONFIG_ROOT instead of the session cwd.
   3. loadPiConfigDetailed uses MAGIC_CONTEXT_CONFIG_ROOT.
   4. configHome honors MAGIC_CONTEXT_CONFIG_HOME.
   5. ensureConfigLocationsMigrated is a no-op in the Fynvra host.
   6. historian response dumps go to MAGIC_CONTEXT_ARTIFACT_DIR.
   7. ensureCortexKitArtifactGitignore does not write into workspaces.
   8. @earendil-works/pi-tui imports (three sites) use the host stub.
   9. src_default reports its storage boot result through the host wrapper; the
      wrapper also exposes boot-ready, so a failed/partial/missing report never
      marks the session as a Magic owner.
  10. historian/dreamer/sidekick reduce nudges are disabled in the Fynvra host.
  11. Fynvra always cancels session_before_compact, including unready/suspended
      bindings. The worker also disables SDK automatic native compaction and
      installs its own cancel hook before attempting plugin startup.
  12. Per-session invalidation: context/session_start/before_agent_start failures
      and exhausted historian retries mark the session suspended, stop context
      transforms/history injection/historian triggers/marker writes, and pause
      the run for explicit recovery. Another session is unaffected. The adapter
      forwards a one-shot warning and aborts unsafe requests; it never enables
      native compaction.
  13. Historian budgets come from the routed current model, using conservative
      UTF-8 byte estimates for text plus framing/output reserves. Whole formatted
      blocks are selected and the complete prompt is checked before sending.
      No XML slicing; unsupported/tiny windows pause for recovery. Upstream scheduler and
      history-decay estimates remain heuristic, not universal token guarantees.
  14. Only validated, committed historian publication reports success to the host.
      Final validation/no-progress/storage failures suspend the session; transient
      requests have bounded retries. Stop/dispose/model changes invalidate the
      operation. SQLite calls, context copies, deferred writes and marker calls
      check the captured async lifetime. Cancellation synchronously releases only
      bookkeeping leases/reservations; no late publication or transcript rewrite.
      Native markers include a cumulative upstream-rendered history snapshot.
  15. SDK facades use empty targets to respect Proxy invariants and bind methods
      to their real receivers. Terminal commands/shortcuts/status persistence are
      not registered; missing/late boot cannot acquire ownership. Host routes,
      readiness and suspension are cleared on disposal without clearing another
      session or a replacement binding.
  16. Host config loads only the fixed generated JSON file, without terminal or
      workspace discovery, substitution, or recovery to unsafe defaults. Private
      DBs never migrate terminal data; tokenizer/cache/overlay/wake-plane discovery
      and unrelated startup backfills are disabled. Optional memory/embedding/git
      search flags are explicit. Schema fencing stays pinned to this vendor version.
  17. Export fynvraIsSessionReady for the host request gate. A context hook must
      return transformed messages; missing results suspend the session rather
      than silently sending raw history. The host rechecks readiness/cancellation
      after SDK context hooks. Explicit recovery reloads the same persisted session
      and runs Magic hooks before resuming; no native compact() unlock is used.
      Fail-closed storage boot also rejects late adoption in the Fynvra host;
      only explicit recovery creates a fresh binding.

When upgrading, re-copy the pinned upstream files and re-apply these hosted
changes, including fynvra-host.js. The compaction, validation, tag/drop, SQLite
schema and session-history implementation remain upstream Magic Context.
